exercise rights that the law gives you independently of this license.

3. Commercial use by for-profit organizations

You may not exercise the permissions in section 2 for a commercial purpose
of a for-profit organization, whether you act as that organization or on
its behalf. A for-profit organization includes a business operated for the
financial benefit of its owners, including a sole proprietorship. Commercial
purposes include operating its business internally, providing client work,
and building, improving, promoting, selling, or hosting its products or
services. Giving a product or service away does not by itself remove its
commercial purpose. Employment by a business does not by itself restrict
independent personal work. Anyone may give or accept optional financial
support for otherwise permitted work. Payment grants no additional rights.

4. Public source for every modification

If you edit the covered software, you must publish the corresponding
source of each modified version in a publicly accessible version-control
repository under this exact license, including the changes you own. This
applies even to local edits, uncommitted or abandoned changes, internal
use, and versions you never distribute or deploy. You may use any public
repository host. No submission to or acceptance by the original project
is required.

Publish within 30 calendar days of making the change, or before you first
distribute the modified version or allow others to use it as a service,
whichever comes first. Multiple changes may be published together if each
modified version can be recovered from the public history on time. Keep
each version freely downloadable without registration for as long as you
distribute it or offer it as a service, and for at least twelve months
after its first publication. Give recipients of a modified version and
users of a modified service an accessible link to its corresponding source.

For a fix whose publication would disclose an unremediated vulnerability,
you may delay source publication until the first public disclosure of the
vulnerability or 90 calendar days after making the fix, whichever comes
first. Use this exception only when necessary for coordinated remediation
and promptly notify the affected maintainer privately. The ordinary
deadline still applies if it would expire later. During the delay you may
privately share the fix with affected maintainers or operators to remediate
the vulnerability. This exception does not apply to unrelated changes.

Corresponding source is the preferred editable form of the covered
software as modified, including the scripts, build instructions and
dependency information needed to reproduce it. Preserve notices and
identify your changes. Where a separately licensed dependency is available
from its publisher, you may identify its source and version. Keep secrets,
personal data and private configuration values out of the public source.
Supply safe placeholders or sample configuration where needed. For all
publication and history requirements, a revision sanitized in this way
satisfies the requirement if its covered code changes remain recoverable.
This license
does not require publishing independent programs, third-party private
material, or user data, or give permission to disclose them.

